\section{Spacecraft–Simulation Coupling Analysis}
\label{sec:spacecraft-simulation-coupling}

\subsection{Overview}
The UAP-01 Uranus Orbiter \& Atmospheric Probe is architected as a
mission-class scientific platform whose observational outputs directly
couple into the Uranus Unprecedented Simulation (UUAS). This chapter
formalizes the bidirectional coupling between spacecraft subsystems and
multi-scale simulation domains, establishing a unified science-control
loop spanning quantum, thermodynamic, magnetohydrodynamic, and
ionospheric physics.

\subsection{Coupling Architecture}
The spacecraft–simulation system is defined by two complementary flows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Forward Coupling:} UUAS informs spacecraft design,
    instrument tuning, trajectory geometry, and probe descent profiles.
    \item \textbf{Reverse Coupling:} Spacecraft telemetry provides
    real-time boundary conditions and validation data for UUAS
    multi-scale solvers.
\end{enumerate}

This establishes a closed-loop scientific architecture.

